# Commit Messages

Keep commits simple: **one line only**. No body, no footer, no bullet lists.

Never add Cursor attribution trailers (or any equivalent), including:
- `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>`
- `Made-with: Cursor`

Do not use `git commit --trailer` for attribution. Commit message must be the subject line only.

## Format

```
<semantic-name>: <commit-message>
```

- `semantic-name`: short type such as `fix`, `feat`, `chore`, `refactor`, `docs`, `test`
- `commit-message`: concise summary of why/what changed (imperative mood preferred)

## Examples

```
# ✅ GOOD
fix: block chat when monthly usage cap hit
feat: add chat model and prompt controls
chore: bump dependencies

# ❌ BAD — multi-line / body
fix: block chat when monthly usage cap hit

Also update the usage UI and tests.

# ❌ BAD — missing semantic prefix
block chat when monthly usage cap hit

# ❌ BAD — too verbose
fix: implement a comprehensive solution to block users from chatting when they have hit their monthly usage cap
```
